  "content": {
    "title": "When does Caitlin Clark play? USA Basketball game schedule, stats in FIBA World Cup Qualifiers",
    "text": "March 16, 2026, 9:20 a.m. ETCaitlin Clark is playing for USA Basketball in the FIBA World Cup Qualifiers in San Juan, Puerto Rico.The U.S. team has a 4-0 record and has already qualified for the World Cup in Berlin, Germany.Clark and Team USA will play their final qualifying game against Spain on Tuesday, March 17, 2026.Indiana Fever star Caitlin Clark showcased her defense with a pair of second-half steals in her first start.Not bad for the 24-year-old Clark, playing her third game after eight months away due to injuries. She's playing with USA Basketball in the FIBA World Cup Qualifiers.She helped the U.S. to a 4-0 record in the group, beating New Zealand, Italy, Puerto Rico and Senegal so far. One game remains against Spain to close the tournament.The U.S. has already qualified for the World Cup, set for September in Berlin, Germany, but it is competing in order to get extra reps for younger players on the national team.Here's how to watch Clark and USA Basketball in their qualifiers.Where to watch Caitlin Clark, USA Basketball vs. Spain tomorrow, Tuesday, March 17, 2026USA holds a 10-0 record over Spain, with the two countries last playing in 2016. USA Basketball will tip off against Spain at 5 p.m. Tuesday, March 17, to finish the qualifying tournament.Watch Caitlin Clark, USA Basketball on Sling!Does Caitlin Clark play today? Caitlin Clark plays in USA vs Spain women's basketball game tomorrow Tuesday, March 17, 2026No, Caitlin Clark does not play today. Caitlin Clark and USA Basketball play Game 5 against Spain at 5 p.m. Tuesday, March 17.Buy Caitlin Clark gear on Fanatics!What time does Caitlin Clark play today? When does USA Basketball play Spain in FIBA World Cup qualifier tomorrow, Tuesday, March 17, 2026?Caitlin Clark and USA Basketball return to action tomorrow against Spain at 5 p.m., Tuesday, March 17.Where is USA Basketball, Caitlin Clark playing in the 2026 FIBA World Cup qualifiers?The tournament is being hosted in San Juan, Puerto Rico.When is Caitlin Clark's next game? When is the next USA Basketball game in 2026 FIBA World Cup qualifiers?The group stage finale, the fifth game of the trip, may be the most competitive for the U.S. They will play Spain at 5 p.m., Tuesday, March 17.Buy Caitlin Clark's Nike merch!Caitlin Clark points, stats, in USA Basketball games at 2026 FIBA World Cup qualifiersIn 19 minutes, Caitlin Clark scored 17 points with 12 assists to two turnovers in a tournament-opening 110-46 win over Senegal on Wednesday. Read more here.Clark's offense was not as effective in her second game, that in as many days after eight months recovering from an injury. She finished with eight points, three rebounds and two assists in the 91-48 win over Puerto Rico on Thursday. Read more here.Clark then looked better in her third game, a 93-59 win over Italy, finishing with 12 points on 4-of-5 shooting with five assists and a steal. There was better flow within the offense, and she even had a steal and a transition bounce pass that threaded the needle for a layup.In the fourth game of the tournament, Clark got her first start with the senior national team. She had 14 points on 6 of 11 shooting (2 of 7 on 3s), a team-high six assists and two steals.USA Basketball results at 2026 FIBA World Cup qualifying tournamentWednesday, March 11: USA 110, Senegal 46. INSIDERThursday, March 12: USA 91, Puerto Rico 48. INSIDERSaturday, March 14: USA 93, Italy 59. INSIDERSunday, March 15: USA 101, New Zealand 46. INSIDERUSA Basketball schedule in 2026 FIBA World Cup qualifying tournamentHere is the full schedule (all times ET):Tuesday, March 17: vs Spain, 5 p.m.Watch Caitlin Clark, USA Basketball live!Chloe Peterson is the Indiana Fever beat reporter for IndyStar. Reach her at capeterson@gannett.com or follow her on X at @chloepeterson67.Get IndyStar's Indiana Fever and Caitlin Clark coverage sent directly to your inbox with our Caitlin Clark Fever newsletter. Subscribe to IndyStar's YouTube channel for Fever Insiders Live.",
